<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14652" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρᾰβος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰρ], ὁ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>gnashing</i> or
			<i>chattering</i> of teeth, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. δὲ διὰ στόμα γίγνετ᾽ ὀδόντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.375
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				404
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				5.3
			</span></i>; prob. 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄραδος</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.654b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>rattling, ringing,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάκεος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Del.</u>
					147
				</span></i>
			. (Prob. onomatop.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
